   pet was an off-brand cat. Re-examined 2026-07-29 when the pet became the
   mascot itself, and KEPT, because the pet is not a standalone sprite: it is
   one actor in a diorama whose every other layer is tofu-scoped. Measured —
   `tofu-scene.js:629` refuses to paint unless `data-theme === 'tofu'`, and the
   ground (`--bar-scene`), the foreground occlusion canvas, the organic top
   edge and the speech bubble are ALL `[data-theme="tofu"]` rules. So on
   dark/light the pet would walk on a bare flat toolbar with no ground, no
   scene lighting and no critter to chase — reading as a sticker pasted on a
   bar, which is the exact "sprite, not inhabitant" failure the brand work
   fought. To surface it on all three themes, port the diorama first (ground +
   fg canvas + lightInfo), not just this one line.

