/* Folder badges — FROSTED-GLASS LOZENGES hung on the diorama.
   Redesign (2026-07): the old "SNES 3D item tag" (a 4-colour hard bevel + a
   `0 2px 0` block drop) read as a pasted game button floating ON the painted
   meadow — the two tells of the "not blended" look. This reworks each chip into
   a frosted-glass CAPSULE that lets the scene blur THROUGH it (blend) while a
   substantial cream frost + a white ink scrim keep the label crisp over the
   busy field (readability). It adopts the bar frame's "gallery-hung painting"
   language: ONE warm hairline (no bevel), soft feathered elevation (no hard
   drop), and a glass-edge inner top highlight. Design research: frosted glass
   needs MORE blur over intricate backgrounds (NN/g); a near-solid protected
   panel + a light text-shadow scrim give per-letter figure-ground separation
   over a busy field (badgezoo / Smashing); an inner light edge is what makes it
   read as real glass (Comeau). The capsule shape also correctly signals a
   TAG/identity chip, distinct from the rounded-rect control buttons. */
