}

/* ── Smooth scroll for reading flow ── */
/* ★ SCROLL-JITTER FIX (2026-07-24): `scroll-behavior:smooth` on the chat
 * container turns every programmatic `scrollTop=scrollHeight` into an
 * animation. During streaming, `updateStreamingUI` writes scrollTop once
 * per rAF while scrollHeight is still GROWING — the smooth animator
 * perpetually chases a moving target, and interacts badly with the
 * `overflow-anchor` primitives above, so the reader visibly drifts off
 * the bottom then snaps back (the reported "generation makes the page
 * scroll up and down on its own"). User-driven wheel / touch / keyboard
 * scroll is always instant per the CSS spec regardless of this property,
 * so dropping the smooth-scroll rule loses nothing perceptible for
 * reading and removes the jitter. `scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})`
 * call sites (branch panel, turn nav) still animate — that behavior is
 * per-call, not inherited from this rule. */
[data-theme="tofu"] .chat-container{
  scroll-behavior:auto
}

/* ── Thinking block — quiet disclosure matching the shared conversation
   chrome: no card frame at all, tertiary label. Reasoning body keeps the
   warm secondary ink only while expanded. ── */
[data-theme="tofu"] .thinking-text{
  font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;font-weight:430;
  font-family:var(--sans-body);
  color:var(--text-secondary)
}
[data-theme="tofu"] .thinking-block{
